INFO:
After decades of distinguished service, Land Rover has retired the legendary Defender and replaced it with a new generation. It was a challenging task, it was to replace a true icon of motoring, still appreciated by many fans. Times are changing and the British manufacturer needed to make a vehicle in step with the times and with increasingly stringent standards both for the protection of occupants in case of accident, and emissions. For Defender there are three very different versions in size, the 90, the 110 and the 130. The aesthetics also change, which to emphasize the sportiness and exclusivity of the model, as well as to support the renewed performance, focuses on widened tracks of 6.8 centimeters. , while the height grows by 2.8 centimetres, allowing the Octa to overcome 1 metre deep fords. The materials chosen for the interior have also been revised, as well as the seats with integrated headrest.

